            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0909" n="829" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.428/1949a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Canada</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-08T16:00:00-04:00">May 8, 1936—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>41. Department’s instruction No. 267 of March 5, 1936, in regard to Halibut
                    Fishery Convention.</p>
                <pb facs="0910" n="830" xml:id="pg830"/>
                <p>Please inform the Department of any changes in draft which may be desired by the
                    Canadian Government. Department would like to have consideration given to
                    inserting the words “except when such violation is committed in the territorial
                    waters of the other party” in line 16 of Article II after “provisions”. If
                    agreement be reached and it be agreeable to the Canadian Government the
                    Department will request the President to issue full power to you to sign the
                    convention at Ottawa.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
